00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:21,280
Let's settle this with 1v1 matches,
best of three.

276
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:23,720
If I win, you have to be my boyfriend

277
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:25,320
until the day of P'Toobtub's wedding.

278
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:27,240
You'll have to do whatever I say.

279
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:29,200
Whatever I want to eat,
you have to get it for me.

280
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:31,280
And whatever I tell you to do,
you have to do it.

281
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:33,360
Whoa!

282
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:35,280
Are you looking for
a boyfriend or a servant?

283
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:36,240
Shut up!

284
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:37,760
What do you say, Soh?

285
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:38,920
If I lose,

286
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:41,320
I'll be your servant for a whole month.

287
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:43,160
Are you up for the duel?

288
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:49,160
PreawSoh! PreawSoh!

289
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:53,560
- PreawSoh! PreawSoh!
- PreawSoh! PreawSoh!

290
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:55,760
- PreawSoh! PreawSoh!
- PreawSoh! PreawSoh!

291
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:58,200
- PreawSoh!
- Oh, come on, just do it.

292
00:15:58,280 --> 00:15:59,880
Just do it for fun, Soh.

293
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:02,120
If you lose, just think of it
as an act of charity for her.

294
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:03,320
I gave up.

295
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,080
I've had enough of you guys.

296
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,920
If you're going to duel,
just get on with it.

297
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:09,440
My girl and I
have some private things to do.

298
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:10,920
Let's go, babe.

299
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:12,400
Come on.

300
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,560
Whoa, right in front of us?

301
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:16,680
Now that he's gone, check this out.

302
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,880
This looks nothing like him, does it?

303
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,360
Laem, you've got a real big mouth.

304
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:30,120
Whoa...

305
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,120
Did you get taller?

306
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:36,600
Well, I guess that's what happens

307
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,040
when time passes.

308
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:40,120
Jeez, listen to you.

309
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:42,120
Talking back
as soon as you get here, huh?

310
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:44,800
- Who'd you get that smart mouth from?
- Stop being a pain in the ass.

311
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,080
If your leg wasn't hurt,

312
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:47,400
I wouldn't have set foot in here.

313
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:50,080
Are you faking it?

314
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:54,320
No! Who would fake it?

315
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:55,680
That's nonsense. Jeez.

316
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,320
Man, my leg is killing me.

317
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:59,040
Help me over to a seat, will you?

318
00:16:59,040 --> 00:16:59,880
Ouch!

319
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:01,320
Fine. Let's go.

320
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:03,760
Whoa!

321
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,080
Just walk, will you?

322
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:06,800
Jeez.

323
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:12,840
What the hell?

324
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,080
Come on, smile.

325
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,280
What?

326
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:24,680
It's just a leg injury.
You're not gonna die.

327
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,360
Mom won't have to
worry about you anymore.

328
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:27,480
- I'm heading back.
- Hey!

329
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:28,600
Wait a minute.

330
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,760
Stay and play a match with me first.

331
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:34,720
I don't play games anymore.

332
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:36,160
Nice try.

333
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:38,400
I just saw you on your story
playing games with your friends.

334
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:39,640
Come on, just one round.

335
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:42,160
First one to lose
or get their tower wrecked

336
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:45,640
is officially the kid Mom and Dad
picked up from a wet trash can.

337
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,800
Come on, one game.

338
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,080
- Fine.
- Hurry up! Let's go.

339
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:07,360
Does Dad still like chatting
with that uncle at the noodle shop?

340
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:09,160
He still does.

341
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:14,320
Does Mom still like
those crispy pancakes?

342
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:15,960
She doesn't eat them anymore.

343
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:17,880
Her blood sugar is too high.

344
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,880
Don't forget to take them
for their checkups.

345
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:28,760
How much longer
do I have to do all this for you?

346
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:33,320
You know Mom and Dad
are getting old, right?

347
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:35,880
They might not be able to wait
until your big day comes.

348
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:36,960
Hey, watch your mouth.

349
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:39,040
I'm serious. I'm not trying to jinx it.

350
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:42,480
I just don't want you
to end up full of regrets later.

351
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:47,040
Yeah, I'm trying.

352
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:51,520
Then step it up!

353
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:54,360
You don't need a car,
a house, or whatever.

354
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:55,840
Just come home once in a while.

355
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:59,440
Let them see
how hard you're actually trying.

356
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:00,920
Is that too much to ask?

357
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:05,280
I won't even talk sh*t to you anymore.

358
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:11,280
I'm putting in the work
for the tournament.

359
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:14,640
This is the first time
my team has a shot at the Top 4.

360
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,840
If we pull it off,

361
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:18,960
ask Mom and Dad to come cheer for us.

362
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:33,440
Ouch!

363
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:34,720
Argh...

364
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:36,480
What?

365
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:41,040
Here.

366
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:43,840
I might not be ready to face them yet,

367
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:45,960
but that doesn't mean I don't care.

368
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,160
Just give these to them for me.

369
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:52,040
What's your angle here?

370
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:53,720
What?

371
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,160
What kind of person
do you think your big brother is?

372
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,640
I actually wanted to buy them something.

373
00:19:57,680 --> 00:19:59,600
I was gonna go with some designer brand,

374
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:01,000
but someone told me...

375
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,440
good things don't have to be expensive.

376
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:07,920
A new lover, I take it?

377
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:09,720
What lover? Shut the f*ck up.

378
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:11,120
You're full of it.

379
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:14,160
Fine, if it's not, it's not.

380
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:15,520
Why are you getting so defensive?

381
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:19,400
What?

382
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:20,760
Is it one-sided love?

383
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:22,160
You dumbass.

384
00:20:22,520 --> 00:20:23,160
Jeez!

385
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:30,760
Why would you even think that?

386
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:32,000
Because a guy like you...

387
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:34,240
could never come up with this idea.

388
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:37,280
You wouldn't listen to anyone's advice

389
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:39,640
unless they were someone important.

390
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:46,440
But it's for the best
that they aren't your partner.

391
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:49,760
We should let decent people
find someone good,

392
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:50,800
shouldn't we?

393
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:05,960
(Preaw has equalized against Soh,
making it 1-1!)

394
00:21:06,040 --> 00:21:08,760
If she manages to beat him,

395
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:10,560
he'll have to be her boyfriend.

396
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:12,080
Nothing can stop this now.

397
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:14,160
- Sh*t!
- (But from what I see,)

398
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:16,000
(it looks like he actually...)

399
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:17,400
- (wants to be her boyfriend)
- What the hell?

400
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:18,320
- (because...)
- Hey, Four,

401
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:19,560
watch my room for a sec.

402
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:21,240
- What?
- I'm in trouble.

403
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:23,120
Where are you going?

404
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:25,280
- I thought you said your leg was hurt.
- Yeah.

405
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:31,560
(Legendary Honor)

406
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:35,000
(Enemies spawning in three seconds.)

407
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:36,320
(All Creeps Deployed)

408
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:42,360
- Whoa.
- Go for it, P'Soh! You can do this.

409
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:47,080
What is he gonna do now?

410
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:47,920
Whoa...

411
00:21:54,520 --> 00:21:56,640
Wait, what's this?
Wow, look at this move.

412
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:58,080
- Here we go.
- Hurry up!

413
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:00,320
He's got to keep his head in the game!

414
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:12,240
Is he trying to lose
so he can be Preaw's boyfriend?

415
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:13,720
He's literally holding back here.

416
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:14,720
Wow,

417
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:23,320
this is so intense!

418
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:30,640
Are you guys taking this
a bit too seriously?

419
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:32,120
You didn't play like this
in the actual tournament.

420
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:34,400
Whoa!

421
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,480
Is this the end?

422
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:53,280
What's going to happen?

423
00:22:53,320 --> 00:22:55,840
Get that! There you go. Now what?

424
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:03,320
Hey, Soh! Wait!

425
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:05,000
Yes, P'Three?

426
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:21,080
Yes! I won!

427
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:29,440
I won!

428
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:42,720
As we agreed, we're a couple now, babe.

429
00:23:43,520 --> 00:23:45,680
Babe, I want some bubble tea.

430
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:48,080
Go get some bubble tea for me.

431
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:49,960
- Bubble tea?
- Bubble tea.

432
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,400
Your girl wants bubble tea,
so what are you gonna do?

433
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:54,920
Uh...

434
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:56,960
Okay.

435
00:23:57,760 --> 00:23:58,800
"Okay, babe."

436
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:00,600
Say it again.

437
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:02,560
"Yes, babe."

438
00:24:03,240 --> 00:24:04,040
Yes...

439
00:24:04,720 --> 00:24:06,200
Yes, babe.

440
00:24:07,760 --> 00:24:11,520
- PreawSoh! PreawSoh!
- PreawSoh! PreawSoh!

441
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:13,240
- PreawSoh! PreawSoh!
- PreawSoh! PreawSoh!

442
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:15,600
- PreawSoh! PreawSoh!
- Where are you going?

443
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:18,360
Let's go get some bubble tea, babe.

444
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:22,400
Aw!

445
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:24,200
- Are they actually serious?
- Oh, my...

446
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:26,200
Why are you sitting there like a statue?

447
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:41,000
(Babe, lead the way for me.)

448
00:24:41,040 --> 00:24:43,680
- (Sure thing, babe.)
- (I'm dying. Heal me, babe!)

449
00:24:43,680 --> 00:24:44,920
(On my way, babe.)

450
00:24:44,920 --> 00:24:46,640
(It's so much fun
playing with you, babe.)

451
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:48,400
(Don't forget to bring some treats
when we meet tomorrow.)

452
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:49,880
(I want strawberry cheesecake,
egg tarts,)

453
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:51,680
(raspberry croissants,
and chocolate macarons.)

454
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:53,360
(Is that all, babe?)

455
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:55,680
(Hello? Where'd you go, Preaw?)

456
00:24:55,680 --> 00:24:58,400
Wait, did I just kick her? Damn.

457
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:02,160
Excuse me, I'll take this one.

458
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:04,200
This one, and that one...
Actually, I'll take them all.

459
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:06,320
What are you doing
buying all these pastries?

460
00:25:07,040 --> 00:25:08,200
You're really taking everything?

461
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:11,200
Oh, yeah. I'm giving them
to underprivileged kids.

462
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:12,760
It's unbelievable

463
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,640
that someone like you
actually does charity work.

464
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:15,720
That's nice.

465
00:25:15,840 --> 00:25:17,640
Is that a compliment?

466
00:25:17,680 --> 00:25:19,560
What are you doing here?
Buying some treats for Preaw?

467
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:21,360
Sorry, though.

468
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:22,800
Looks like she's out of luck.

469
00:25:23,840 --> 00:25:25,000
It's alright.

470
00:25:25,280 --> 00:25:27,520
I'll just take her out
to dinner instead.

471
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:28,240
What?

472
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:29,440
Just the two of you?

473
00:25:37,200 --> 00:25:38,680
Then I'll just give these to you

474
00:25:38,720 --> 00:25:40,400
so you don't have to pay for them.

475
00:25:40,680 --> 00:25:42,800
Wow, you're so kind.

476
00:25:43,360 --> 00:25:44,160
Thank you so much.

477
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:47,280
This cake looks so good.

478
00:25:47,960 --> 00:25:49,120
It's so yummy, babe.

479
00:25:49,160 --> 00:25:49,960
"Babe"?

480
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:51,560
Damn, "babe."

481
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:54,480
Hey, what the hell was that for?

482
00:25:55,120 --> 00:25:56,000
Is it good?

483
00:25:56,400 --> 00:25:57,120
It is.

484
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:57,840
Babe...

485
00:25:58,360 --> 00:26:00,520
I feel a bit sore here.
Give me a massage.

486
00:26:00,640 --> 00:26:01,480
Okay.

487
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:03,560
Hey, hey!

488
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,480
She needs to get it from me.

489
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:10,840
Feels good, huh?

490
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:12,880
Yeah, that's nice.

491
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:15,240
Whoa, that feels great.

492
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:16,480
Great?

493
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:18,280
I can do even better.

494
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:20,760
What are you so satisfied about?

495
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:26,440
That's enough.

496
00:26:27,760 --> 00:26:28,640
I'm all relaxed now.

497
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:30,720
Babe, finish this, too.

498
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:32,200
I'm leaving.

499
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:37,320
Is her back made of steel or something?

500
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:38,640
It's hard as hell.

501
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:49,440
Do you know...

502
00:26:49,560 --> 00:26:51,560
just how important your hands are
to the team?

503
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:55,800
You need to take better care of them.

504
00:27:16,520 --> 00:27:19,400
Babe, I want that piece of pork.
Can you get it for me?

505
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:22,600
I can't reach it.
Babe, please get it for me.

506
00:27:22,800 --> 00:27:23,520
Sure.

507
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:25,160
Hey!

508
00:27:26,160 --> 00:27:27,320
Eat it yourself for once.

509
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:30,320
You keep feeding someone else.

510
00:27:30,400 --> 00:27:33,240
But that piece was mine, P'Three!

511
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:35,400
There, there. It's okay.

512
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:37,080
Here, this could cheer you up.

513
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:37,720
Here.

514
00:27:37,720 --> 00:27:40,120
Gosh, keep that for yourself.

515
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:41,360
It's pure fat.

516
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:49,000
Hey, that piece was mine!

517
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:50,240
You've eaten plenty already.

518
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:51,600
Let him have some, too.

519
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:53,800
Look at him. He's so thin... Aw!

520
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:55,480
He's practically skin and bones.

521
00:28:01,720 --> 00:28:03,960
Oh, babe, I'm out of my drink.

522
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:05,760
Please refill it for me.

523
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:07,120
Sure.

524
00:28:07,760 --> 00:28:09,160
I'll go get it for you.

525
00:28:09,440 --> 00:28:10,560
You're the sweetest.

526
00:28:12,960 --> 00:28:14,960
Do you ever plan on
doing anything for yourself?

527
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:40,040
Let me help.

528
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:44,240
I've seen you running around
doing things all day.

529
00:28:55,560 --> 00:28:56,760
Seriously though, Soh.

530
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:59,000
Why did you agree
to be Preaw's boyfriend?

531
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:03,240
Well...

532
00:29:03,920 --> 00:29:05,480
You told me once

533
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:07,160
that you've spent all your time

534
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:08,960
on gaming and studying.

535
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:11,080
So why are you making time for her, too?

536
00:29:13,400 --> 00:29:14,760
I just wanted to know

537
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:17,000
what it's like to love
and take care of someone

538
00:29:17,040 --> 00:29:18,720
just like you said.

539
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:22,520
Oh, Derpy Kid.

540
00:29:22,760 --> 00:29:25,080
How can you be so derpy? Seriously.

541
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:31,840
So, how is it? Does it feel good?

542
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:33,480
Well...

543
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:35,320
I guess so.

544
00:29:36,520 --> 00:29:37,840
Yeah, good for you.

545
00:29:38,280 --> 00:29:40,960
God, Three,
what the hell did you just say?

546
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:42,920
Good for you?

547
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:44,320
How could you say that?

548
00:29:46,520 --> 00:29:47,680
You think so?

549
00:29:57,720 --> 00:30:00,600
To be honest,
I'm not really sure...

550
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:06,120
what those feelings actually mean.

551
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:10,080
And...

552
00:30:10,960 --> 00:30:12,920
does your heart race
when you're with Preaw?

553
00:30:13,280 --> 00:30:14,200
It does, sometimes.

554
00:30:23,040 --> 00:30:24,520
Like when we play games together.

555
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:25,560
Anyway,

556
00:30:26,520 --> 00:30:28,800
I'm just not sure

557
00:30:28,840 --> 00:30:32,520
what a racing heart like that
is supposed to mean.

558
00:30:35,880 --> 00:30:37,280
I just want to be sure

559
00:30:38,480 --> 00:30:40,480
because I don't want anyone
to get hurt because of me.

560
00:31:03,440 --> 00:31:04,200
Sorry.

561
00:31:31,880 --> 00:31:32,600
Mom,

562
00:31:33,680 --> 00:31:34,840
my bike broke down.

563
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:37,040
I'll probably look
for a repair shop around here.

564
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:38,920
I'll be home a bit late, Mom.

565
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:43,760
(Oh, is that Ten?)

566
00:31:44,480 --> 00:31:45,720
Are you two together?

567
00:31:45,880 --> 00:31:46,920
Hello, Mom.

568
00:31:47,120 --> 00:31:48,400
Wow, it's been a long time.

569
00:31:48,600 --> 00:31:49,720
You've become even prettier.

570
00:31:50,280 --> 00:31:52,720
(My, still as sweet-talking as ever.)

571
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:55,000
(Seeing you two like this,
I'm not worried anymore.)

572
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:58,280
(Please bring Jack home, okay, Ten?)

573
00:31:58,720 --> 00:31:59,600
It's fine, Mom.

574
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:00,920
- I'll call a ride...
- Sure, Mom.

575
00:32:01,040 --> 00:32:02,120
I'll take Jack home myself.

576
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:08,720
Just leave your bike here.

577
00:32:08,960 --> 00:32:10,600
I'll text a mechanic
to come fix it for you.

578
00:32:11,880 --> 00:32:13,200
I said I'd go home myself.

579
00:32:13,760 --> 00:32:14,880
If your ears are working fine,

580
00:32:15,080 --> 00:32:16,360
you should've heard what I just said.

581
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:19,320
But your mom entrusted you to me.

582
00:32:19,720 --> 00:32:21,000
If you're not an idiot,

583
00:32:21,560 --> 00:32:22,600
you should've heard that, too.

584
00:32:24,080 --> 00:32:24,920
I heard it.

585
00:32:26,080 --> 00:32:27,560
But I didn't ask for your help.

586
00:32:31,960 --> 00:32:33,160
Fine, whatever.

587
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:34,960
If you want to walk home in the rain,
suit yourself.

588
00:32:43,040 --> 00:32:43,960
Jeez!

589
00:32:45,320 --> 00:32:46,120
What the hell?

590
00:32:57,080 --> 00:32:57,960
Are you happy now?

591
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,680
Happy?

592
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:00,840
With what?

593
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:03,160
You should be saying,

594
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:07,360
"I'm sorry to trouble you, Mr. Ten."
That would be more like it.

595
00:33:19,360 --> 00:33:20,280
Oh, my goodness!

596
00:33:20,280 --> 00:33:21,120
I'm home, Mom.

597
00:33:21,160 --> 00:33:22,280
You're both soaking wet.

598
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:23,960
Wait.

599
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:27,640
Here you go.

600
00:33:28,960 --> 00:33:29,680
Thank you.

601
00:33:29,760 --> 00:33:30,760
Sorry to trouble you, Mom.

602
00:33:31,040 --> 00:33:32,320
It's no trouble at all.

603
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:34,480
I should be thanking you, actually,

604
00:33:34,560 --> 00:33:36,040
for bringing Jack home.

605
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:39,000
Since you're already here,
stay for dinner with us.

606
00:33:39,320 --> 00:33:40,760
I made plenty of food.

607
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:41,440
Mom,

608
00:33:41,840 --> 00:33:42,760
Ten is busy.

609
00:33:42,840 --> 00:33:44,480
- He has tons of work.
- I'm not busy, Mom.

610
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:45,760
Not at all.

611
00:33:46,080 --> 00:33:48,520
I missed your cooking
more than anything in the world.

612
00:33:48,560 --> 00:33:49,880
You're such a sweet talker.

613
00:33:50,360 --> 00:33:52,760
Jack, go take a shower.

614
00:33:53,040 --> 00:33:54,640
Hurry back for dinner. Go on.

615
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:57,320
Hurry up and change so we can eat.

616
00:33:57,600 --> 00:33:59,320
Come on. Go on.

617
00:33:59,920 --> 00:34:00,800
Follow me.

618
00:34:16,240 --> 00:34:16,920
Here.

619
00:34:24,120 --> 00:34:25,880
Still got no shame, I see.

620
00:34:27,400 --> 00:34:28,160
Why should I be embarrassed?

621
00:34:28,480 --> 00:34:29,480
We're both guys.

622
00:34:33,080 --> 00:34:34,000
Or is it bothering you?

623
00:34:36,920 --> 00:34:37,880
Put it on.

624
00:34:44,840 --> 00:34:46,000
You still kept this?

625
00:34:49,040 --> 00:34:51,160
I threw mine in the trash ages ago.

626
00:34:52,960 --> 00:34:55,200
I'm not surprised.
Not with someone like you.

627
00:35:20,400 --> 00:35:22,320
Take some food home, Ten.

628
00:35:22,680 --> 00:35:23,760
Thank you, Mom.

629
00:35:23,960 --> 00:35:25,680
And don't worry about your clothes.

630
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:26,960
I'll take care of them

631
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:28,960
and have Jack return them to you.

632
00:35:29,520 --> 00:35:30,400
Thank you.

633
00:35:31,080 --> 00:35:33,520
Mom, your cooking
is still as amazing as ever.

634
00:35:34,160 --> 00:35:35,720
It reminds me of the old days,

635
00:35:36,120 --> 00:35:36,760
right?

636
00:35:37,600 --> 00:35:39,720
If you miss my cooking,
come visit more often.

637
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:41,400
Ugh, no need, Mom.

638
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:43,240
He's busy as hell.

639
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,960
- Don't bother him.
- I'm not busy at all.

640
00:35:45,600 --> 00:35:48,360
I promise to come visit Jack more often.

641
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:52,280
I didn't bring anything with me today.

642
00:35:52,960 --> 00:35:55,520
Next time,
I'll definitely bring something.

643
00:35:56,240 --> 00:35:57,240
I'm heading out now.

644
00:35:57,480 --> 00:35:58,280
Goodbye, Mom.

645
00:35:59,080 --> 00:36:00,880
- I'm off.
- Just get lost.

646
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:16,240
(Remember that old friend
I told you about?)

647
00:36:16,480 --> 00:36:19,040
(Ran into him today.
He's annoying as hell.)

648
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:25,040
(Tell me about it.)

649
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:29,360
(It's a long story.)

650
00:36:29,360 --> 00:36:30,800
(Can we meet up sometime?)

651
00:36:31,120 --> 00:36:31,960
(Okay.)

652
00:36:45,840 --> 00:36:46,960
Why did you ask me to come?

653
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:51,760
How can you be certain

654
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:54,280
that you actually like someone?

655
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:55,720
Why are you asking that?

656
00:36:56,320 --> 00:36:57,720
You're acting like
you've never dated someone.

657
00:36:58,440 --> 00:37:00,440
It's just like
however you felt with your ex.

658
00:37:00,920 --> 00:37:02,560
It's not the same.

659
00:37:03,040 --> 00:37:04,320
How is it different?

660
00:37:05,040 --> 00:37:05,960
Or...

661
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:07,640
is it a guy this time?

662
00:37:11,560 --> 00:37:13,720
Even if it is,
there's nothing wrong with it.

663
00:37:14,200 --> 00:37:15,280
Feelings...

664
00:37:15,440 --> 00:37:17,280
don't choose who they happen to.

665
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:20,280
Even people who have never met before

666
00:37:20,880 --> 00:37:21,960
can develop feelings

667
00:37:22,520 --> 00:37:23,760
for each other just by talking.

668
00:37:24,480 --> 00:37:26,640
Yeah, I know.
I'm not worried about that.

669
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:27,760
It's just...

670
00:37:28,440 --> 00:37:30,000
there's this thin line.

671
00:37:30,760 --> 00:37:33,440
I don't know
what this feeling really is.

672
00:37:34,320 --> 00:37:35,200
Do I...

673
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:37,880
like him as someone I could love,

674
00:37:38,680 --> 00:37:39,440
or...

675
00:37:40,080 --> 00:37:42,200
is it just brotherly affection?

676
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:52,560
I'm afraid if I cross that line,

677
00:37:54,960 --> 00:37:56,400
I'll no longer be P'Three in his eyes.

678
00:37:58,080 --> 00:37:59,240
I'll just be a f*cking jerk named Three.

679
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:06,280
I get you, Three.

680
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:08,760
Maybe you've just been single
for a while

681
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:12,640
and forgotten what it feels like
to like someone.

682
00:38:14,840 --> 00:38:17,640
How can I be sure, then?

683
00:38:28,800 --> 00:38:29,920
What are you doing?

684
00:38:30,560 --> 00:38:31,720
What the hell are you doing?

685
00:38:32,080 --> 00:38:33,760
Are you crazy?
What are you trying to do?

686
00:38:33,800 --> 00:38:34,720
I'm proving it.

687
00:38:37,560 --> 00:38:39,280
See? It hasn't even been a minute,

688
00:38:39,480 --> 00:38:40,400
and you already pulled away.

689
00:38:40,880 --> 00:38:42,640
That means you don't like me.

690
00:38:42,680 --> 00:38:44,840
Of course I don't! It's just so wrong.

691
00:38:45,040 --> 00:38:45,720
Yeah.

692
00:38:46,560 --> 00:38:47,440
Give it a shot.

693
00:38:47,720 --> 00:38:49,320
Try holding that person's hand.

694
00:38:50,440 --> 00:38:52,640
See if you can last for a whole minute.

695
00:38:53,440 --> 00:38:54,880
With someone you don't like,

696
00:38:55,600 --> 00:38:56,400
even a second

697
00:38:57,240 --> 00:38:58,160
feels like forever.

698
00:38:59,360 --> 00:39:00,760
But with someone you actually like,

699
00:39:01,960 --> 00:39:03,360
even if it's a full minute,

700
00:39:04,640 --> 00:39:06,160
it flies by so damn fast.

701
00:39:39,680 --> 00:39:40,440
P'Three!

702
00:39:41,520 --> 00:39:42,440
Where are you going?

703
00:39:45,120 --> 00:39:46,880
Hey, where are you going?

704
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:47,960
Hey, wait!

705
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:50,200
Here, I bought you some snacks.

706
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:53,000
Is something wrong with your head?

707
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:54,480
- You?
- Yeah.

708
00:39:55,160 --> 00:39:56,240
Or did you put laxatives in here?

709
00:39:56,320 --> 00:39:57,480
Are you crazy?

710
00:39:57,600 --> 00:39:58,800
I went out of my way to bring you this.

711
00:39:59,120 --> 00:40:00,240
Fine, don't take it.

712
00:40:01,600 --> 00:40:03,080
But if you don't,

713
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:06,320
you'll never find out the tea

714
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:08,280
about Preaw and Soh

715
00:40:08,480 --> 00:40:11,200
that my ears just happened to overhear.

716
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:12,760
- I'm out. See ya.
- Hey!

717
00:40:13,240 --> 00:40:14,360
Get over here.

718
00:40:14,520 --> 00:40:15,120
What?

719
00:40:15,520 --> 00:40:16,160
- What?
- Come here.

720
00:40:19,160 --> 00:40:20,560
Whatever you heard, tell me everything.

721
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:26,120
So, here we go.

722
00:40:28,680 --> 00:40:29,480
I'm telling you

723
00:40:29,480 --> 00:40:32,240
if you saw the way Praew looked at Soh,

724
00:40:32,600 --> 00:40:34,280
you'd know she's serious.
They've even got

725
00:40:34,320 --> 00:40:36,320
- their first date planned.
- Soh...

726
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:37,880
Where did P'Three go?

727
00:40:39,120 --> 00:40:41,640
He should be in the back,

728
00:40:41,680 --> 00:40:42,600
putting things away.

729
00:40:46,200 --> 00:40:47,320
Soh,

730
00:40:47,960 --> 00:40:49,320
do you know what day tomorrow is?

731
00:40:51,280 --> 00:40:52,680
It's Saturday.

732
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:59,160
And do you know
what couples do on Saturdays?

733
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:02,920
Can you just tell me? I've never been
in a relationship before.

734
00:41:07,160 --> 00:41:09,840
Straight up, there's a new movie out
this Saturday.

735
00:41:10,320 --> 00:41:11,320
I want to go see it.

736
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:12,600
Will you go see it with me?

737
00:41:13,400 --> 00:41:15,120
You will, right?
You're buying me popcorn, too.

738
00:41:15,120 --> 00:41:15,840
It's a deal.

739
00:41:25,280 --> 00:41:26,760
She's totally using him for free food.

740
00:41:27,480 --> 00:41:28,800
Trying to milk him dry?

741
00:41:30,560 --> 00:41:33,120
Why are you telling me this?
I don't care at all.

742
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:34,560
It's their business, isn't it?

743
00:41:34,680 --> 00:41:36,320
Oh, really?

744
00:41:41,200 --> 00:41:42,760
The reason I'm telling you this is...

745
00:41:43,120 --> 00:41:44,640
I just feel bad for Soh.

746
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:46,960
Just think about it.

747
00:41:47,440 --> 00:41:50,960
A man and a woman
going to the movies together.

748
00:41:51,480 --> 00:41:52,560
Just the two of them

749
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:55,040
in a dark theater.

750
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:57,160
It's cold in there.

751
00:41:57,480 --> 00:41:58,600
Soh is no match for Preaw's moves.

752
00:41:58,600 --> 00:41:59,760
Just imagine what those two might do.

753
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:01,280
- Maybe an oil change?
- That's a possibility.

754
00:42:01,320 --> 00:42:02,160
Are you nuts?

755
00:42:02,200 --> 00:42:03,760
- What?
- Whether they go camping, fishing,

756
00:42:03,760 --> 00:42:06,160
or whatever,
it has nothing to do with me.

757
00:42:07,160 --> 00:42:09,480
Now read my lips and remember this.

758
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:12,840
I do not care!

759
00:42:13,440 --> 00:42:14,240
Keep that in mind.

760
00:42:54,760 --> 00:42:56,280
- Holy sh*t!
- Sh*t! What?

761
00:42:56,400 --> 00:42:57,120
What is it?

762
00:43:00,440 --> 00:43:02,360
Whoa...

763
00:43:03,280 --> 00:43:05,680
Bro, you've got it pretty bad.

764
00:43:06,040 --> 00:43:06,800
What?

765
00:43:07,040 --> 00:43:09,200
And why are you even here?

766
00:43:09,240 --> 00:43:10,760
Why are you here?

767
00:43:10,800 --> 00:43:11,920
I thought you said you didn't care.

768
00:43:13,320 --> 00:43:15,000
I'm here for a movie, obviously.

769
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:18,360
Don't you have a movie theater
near your place or something?

770
00:43:18,600 --> 00:43:20,560
I was just bored.

771
00:43:20,640 --> 00:43:23,400
- I just wanted to be somewhere different.
- Oh... Hey, Soh!

772
00:43:27,640 --> 00:43:28,560
Seriously, though.

773
00:43:28,560 --> 00:43:30,360
You're here
because you're jealous of Soh, right?

774
00:43:30,560 --> 00:43:31,120
What?

775
00:43:32,440 --> 00:43:33,920
Me? Jealous of Soh?

776
00:43:34,840 --> 00:43:36,440
I told you I'm here to watch a movie.

777
00:43:38,040 --> 00:43:39,240
You're good at acting cool,

778
00:43:40,800 --> 00:43:41,840
but your face gives you away.

779
00:43:44,560 --> 00:43:45,760
You're not a kid anymore.

780
00:43:46,160 --> 00:43:47,360
It's so obvious.

781
00:43:47,560 --> 00:43:50,440
The way you look at and treat him

782
00:43:50,840 --> 00:43:52,120
goes way beyond brotherly affection.

783
00:43:52,440 --> 00:43:55,080
I think deep down, you already know.

784
00:43:57,760 --> 00:44:00,880
But if you want to keep things
strictly brotherly,

785
00:44:00,880 --> 00:44:01,920
then suit yourself.

786
00:44:03,120 --> 00:44:04,720
Just let Preaw have him.

787
00:44:04,880 --> 00:44:05,520
I'm off.

788
00:44:05,960 --> 00:44:07,840
- Wait.
- What?

789
00:44:14,840 --> 00:44:16,280
The trailers are almost over.

790
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:17,760
I'm going to the restroom real quick.

791
00:44:17,920 --> 00:44:18,480
Okay.

792
00:44:18,520 --> 00:44:19,880
I'll leave this right here.

793
00:44:21,960 --> 00:44:23,800
- You can wait here.
- Okay.

794
00:44:24,480 --> 00:44:25,320
I'll be right back.

795
00:44:31,480 --> 00:44:32,280
P'Cher?

796
00:44:32,600 --> 00:44:33,440
What are you doing here?

797
00:44:37,880 --> 00:44:39,120
Well, the thing is...

798
00:44:39,640 --> 00:44:40,320
I mean...

799
00:44:42,640 --> 00:44:45,200
I'm here to ask you
to the movies, sweetie.

800
00:44:45,400 --> 00:44:46,560
Ew!

801
00:44:46,800 --> 00:44:48,400
Did you fall and hit your head?

802
00:44:48,720 --> 00:44:51,120
I'm here with Soh today.

803
00:44:52,600 --> 00:44:54,280
Not even a second thought?

804
00:44:54,360 --> 00:44:55,920
I went out of my way to ask, you know.

805
00:44:56,680 --> 00:44:57,920
Be serious.

806
00:44:57,960 --> 00:45:00,400
It's obvious you're making things up.
Just spit it out.

807
00:45:01,080 --> 00:45:02,000
Fine, I give up.

808
00:45:02,600 --> 00:45:03,480
Look,

809
00:45:04,800 --> 00:45:05,960
here's the thing.

810
00:45:17,000 --> 00:45:18,360
Hello, Laem?

811
00:45:18,560 --> 00:45:20,720
What? Preaw?

812
00:45:20,760 --> 00:45:22,920
I thought she was all innocent.

813
00:45:25,080 --> 00:45:25,800
Huh?

814
00:45:25,880 --> 00:45:26,960
Preaw?

815
00:45:26,960 --> 00:45:29,320
Hey, seriously?
You have a crush on Preaw?

816
00:45:33,080 --> 00:45:34,200
